    {
      "id": "graph-validity-section-1",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Nodes, graphs and the workspace",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": -640
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "Nodes, graphs and the workspace",
        "body": "A **graph** is a file with one root and a graph id of its own. The root is the node the graph begins from.\n\nA **node** is one thing, known by its node id: a Content node, a Port, a Portal, a Method, or the root of a graph. Most nodes sit in one graph.\n\nA node can also be spread across two files, by expansion. The host file holds a stand-in for the node: an import marked `mode: expand` that names the other file and carries the node's id. The other file holds the node's own parts under a root that carries the same id and is marked as a fragment. The stand-in and the id together make it one node; two files that only share an id are not. Today the fragment's file is the node's home, and edits go back to it. Using one fragment in several graphs is designed and not built.\n\nFrom outside, in another graph, through a Portal or in the workspace, a graph is seen as a node: one of the faces it offers. From inside, it is the graph: its nodes and edges, its ground and its membrane.\n\nThe **workspace** is not a graph. It is where nodes and graphs are arranged. It has no root and is not a file. Graphs selected in it can be rooted: the new graph has its own root and a Portal for each graph selected, and the selected graphs are referenced, not copied.\n\nOne root per file. Two roots in one file is wrong. The root of a fragment, brought into the host to edit a piece of it, is marked informational and is not counted.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "graph-validity"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
